- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests`

**How to implement.** The app imports its catalogues on every start (001 §B 'Import on every start'; .spec-md §0.1 `AppContext.create`: it imports the catalogues on start; §3.7, §3.8; the S3.1 brief: the rows that need a choice are held in the AppContext for S3.2's dialog). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: the record gains two fields, each with a one-line doc. `catalogueImports : CatalogueImportContext` is the library's import seam over the database, through which the Library window registers folders. `pendingImports : PendingCatalogueImport list` holds the start-up imports whose rows wait for a choice. `compose` (step 89) builds `catalogueImports = CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInDatabase database)` (steps 95, 98). It runs `catalogueImports.importOnStart (CatalogueProxy.builtInFolderUnder locations.shippedCatalogueFolder)` (step 92) on every start, created or opened, so step 88's `CreatedLibraryDatabase` branch and its import are deleted. An `Error e` is logged with `Logger.logError` carrying `e.describe` and leaves `pendingImports` empty. For an `Ok report`, every folder report whose outcome is an `Error e` is logged naming the folder and `e.describe`, and `pendingImports` is `report.pending`. The app MUST start with its held database state and pending decisions; no new catalogue row is applied before the Launcher confirms it. `create`'s and `recreateLibrary`'s docs say, in no more words, that every start imports the shipped catalogue and the registered folders by manifest hash. `LibraryDatabase.origin` (step 84) keeps its members, because the facts in `LibraryDatabaseTests` and the backup suites still read it. (2) `AGENTS.md`, the gotcha 'The Main scene's Library is LIVE': the parenthesis naming `CatalogueImportProxy.importFrom` (step 58) names `CatalogueImportContext.importOnStart`, which imports `Catalogue/Builtin/` and every registered catalogue folder on every start. (3) Tests, in `AppContextTests`. Each uses `TestAppScope.fileLocations` (step 88) of the module, with `shippedCatalogueFolder` set to a fresh folder under the test output. That folder's `Builtin` subfolder is written through `CatalogueProxy.create` (step 33) from `BuiltinCatalogue.catalogueData ()`. `create imports a changed shipped catalogue on the next start and skips an unchanged one`: the first create lists Silicon with its description. The `Builtin` folder is rewritten with Silicon's version 2, whose description differs and whose name, and so file name, is unchanged. The second create's `materials.tryGetMaterial MaterialIds.silicon` answers the new description, and `resolveVersion` of version 1 answers the old one. A third create over the unchanged folder leaves the Built-in row of `catalogueImports.proxy.loggedImports ()` exactly as the second create logged it. `create holds every changed-catalogue row pending and writes nothing before confirmation`. After the first create, a user material named `Lab glass` is saved through its `materials`. The `Builtin` folder is rewritten with a new-id material named `Lab glass` and a new source added, both under `BuiltInProvenance CatalogueIds.builtInCatalogue`. The second create's pendingImports MUST hold one catalogue with every row, including the collision, reuse rows and the new source; neither the new material nor the source is held and the import log is unchanged. The step-88 facts `create imports the Built-in catalogue into a new library database file and a reopen does not import again` and `create imports the Built-in catalogue into empty stores` keep their assertions, because an unchanged manifest is skipped. Each AppContext fixture that needs a populated catalogue MUST explicitly settle every pending import before reading its library. The first-create, changed-version and reopen facts MUST assert no entry/log mutation before settlement, then retain their original post-confirmation values and counts. Startup MUST never invoke that fixture confirmation path. In OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TestAppScope.fs, freshAppContext MUST explicitly settle every pending catalogue with its full default choice list before returning a populated test context. Tests of unconfirmed startup MUST call AppContext.create directly. File-backed fixtures MUST use the same explicit sequence; product composition MUST never call this test helper.

**Acceptance.** After the wiring, `AppContext.create` MUST run `importOnStart` over the shipped catalogue on every start and hold its awaiting rows in `pendingImports`, and `AppContext.fs` MUST NOT read `LibraryDatabase.origin`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `create imports a changed shipped catalogue on the next start and skips an unchanged one` and `create holds every changed-catalogue row pending and writes nothing before confirmation`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass. All import rows, including Reuse, MUST require explicit confirmation before library or import-log mutation; an unchanged catalogue manifest or a kit with no snapshots is the only applicable bypass.
